course: dictionary
lesson: 11455
title: Formal words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Administer» is a formal word, the kind you meet in letters, rules and exams. It usually means to run something, or to give something out in a proper, organised way. The clues tell you which meaning fits: a school office, a nurse, a judge.
explain: «The nurse administered the medicine carefully.» A nurse gives medicine to a patient. So administered means gave, but carefully and properly. Try the swap: "The nurse gave the medicine carefully" still makes sense, so you know you have the right idea.
explain: «The school office administers all the trips.» Here the office is in charge of the trips. It plans them, books them and makes sure they run. Here administers means runs or manages. The same word can mean different things, so always check the clues around it.
explain: Health and safety matters too. Only trained people or parents should administer medicine to children. This shows that administer is serious: it means giving something to someone in a careful, correct way, not just handing it over.
fact: Administer means to manage or be in charge of something, such as a school, a test or money.
fact: To administer medicine or first aid means to give it to someone.
fact: To administer a punishment means to give it out. To administer a test or an oath means to give it to people and see that it is done properly.
fact: Administer is a formal word. In everyday talk, people often use run or give instead.
fact: Useful phrases: administer first aid, administer medicine, administer a test, administer justice.
exercise: «The school office administers all the trips.» What does administers mean here? | Loses the keys | Paints the walls | Eats the lunch | * Runs and manages
exercise: «The nurse administered the medicine carefully.» What does administered mean? | Hid the medicine in a drawer | Threw the medicine away | Mixed the medicine with juice | * Gave the medicine to someone properly
exercise: Which word could replace administer in «The head teacher will administer the spelling test»? | * gave | painted | hid | lost
test: Why should only trained people or parents administer medicine to children? | Because medicine tastes nicer when adults give it | * Because it must be given safely and correctly | Because it is only sold on Tuesdays | Because children are not allowed to touch anything
test: What does it mean to administer an oath? | To forget the words of an oath | To shout an oath across a playground | * To give the oath to people and see that it is done properly | To write a poem about an oath
exam: Which meaning of administer fits best in the phrase «administer justice»? | * Carry out fairly | Hide | Stop | Forget
